  "description": "Participants who have not visited Xi'an see 18 street photos in random order: nine control photos of culture and leisure walking streets, traffic lanes and commercial pedestrian streets in central Xi'an and the same nine views with digitally added greenery at three scales. Each photo stays at least 10 s and is rated on the study's eight 5-point word pairs (pleasure: repulsive–nice, tense–restful, uncomfortable–comfortable, unpleasant–pleasant; arousal: monotonous–exciting, inactive–active, boring–interesting, fearful–safe). Rebuilt from Zhang, Wang, Li, Chang & Lu (2022), IJERPH 19(24): 16918, with the paper's Figure 1 photos (CC BY 4.0). Analysis: pleasure and arousal means per photo; paired t-tests treatment vs control; mixed model with treatment dummy, image fixed effects and participant random intercept; split by scale and street type.",
